    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0199" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg75"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A41a/20b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>)<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d91-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-28T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>566. Conference on Limitation of Armament. My 531, September 10, 3 p.m. Inform
                    Foreign Office that Government of United States desires to make following
                    suggestion regarding agenda: Under topic 3 of Pacific and Far Eastern questions,
                    viz., Mandated Islands, to include as Subject A, “Electrical Communications in
                    the Pacific.”</p>
                <p>Repeat to Rome as no. 157 and Paris as no. 441.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d91-f1" n="82" type="source" xml:id="d91-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph for instructions to repeat to Rome (no. 157) and Paris (no.
                    441). The same telegram, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to Tokyo
                    (no. 166) with instructions to repeat to Peking as Department’s no. 266 (file
                    no. 500.A41a/20a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
